# The build context is this directory, and the image must contain only the binary plus
# an example config and an example passwd file (§2.3). Everything the Go build does not
# read is excluded, so nothing can reach the image by accident.

.git
.DS_Store
*.log

# The test corpus. §2.3 bars it from the image; excluding it from the context as well
# keeps a fixture hostname out of every build layer (I2).
fixtures/

# Documentation, the deployment example, and the sidecar example. The image ships the
# config and passwd examples only.
*.md
compose.yml
.labview.example
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# An operator's real config, if they mounted one here.
config/
config.local.yml

# A binary from a local `go build ./cmd/labview`, which writes ./labview into this
# directory — whose name collides with the directory itself, hence the leading slash.
# It is host-native and would be shipped over the one the image builds if it reached
# the context.
/labview
/labview.exe

# There is no frontend build stage and nothing here to exclude for one. What the
# binary serves is the bundle under internal/webui/dist, which is committed and
# embedded by `go:embed` at compile time (§2.2) — so the Go build is the whole build,
# and `go build` and `go test` work in a checkout with no Node installed.
